## `weixin,origin` = DOUBLE delivery when origin is also weixin (2026-09-09 — real root cause of the recurring rate-limit)
The morning rate-limit was NOT just "several crons near-simultaneous". Two deeper bugs amplified it into an all-morning outage:
- **`deliver: weixin,origin` delivers TWICE when origin also points at the same WeChat account.** Check `jobs.json`: 每小时(51814bf28ed7)/收盘前(91df35c579fb)/止损(aa6316b0b52f) all had `origin.platform == 'weixin'` with the SAME `chat_id` as the "weixin" home channel → every trigger sent 2 messages to the same chat (doubles quota burn). This is DIFFERENT from the webui-origin bug above (dead target) — here the second target is live and silently DUPLICATES the message.
- **Rate-limit avalanche / self-locking retry loop**: first cron failure → Hermes fires a plain-text FALLBACK send (each message double-sends) AND enters a ~60s infinite retry loop (log shows `[Weixin] send failed ... cooldown active for 30.0s` every 60s for HOURS, paired with `weixin: restored 1 context token(s)`). The retry loop keeps refreshing iLink's 30s cooldown, so every LATER cron (09:25 DSA, 10:03/11:03 hourly) ALSO fails — one 09:05 miss cascades into a full-morning outage.
- **Diagnose**: `grep "rate limited" ~/.hermes/profiles/main/logs/gateway.log | grep <date>` — a repeating every-60s pair of failures = retry-loop avalanche (vs a one-off cluster = pure stagger problem).
- **Fix applied 2026-09-09**: (1) all 5 report/control crons' deliver changed from `weixin,origin` to explicit single channel `weixin:o9cq80_QqkAnltK8A4P60TrUwZGk@im.wechat` (halves quota burn + kills dead origin targets); (2) DeepSeek余额 9:05 → 8:05 (out of the 9:00-9:30 cluster). Resulting morning line: 8:05余额 / 8:20美股 / 8:45日历(静默) / 9:00定投(静默) / 9:25 DSA / 10:03每小时.
- **Rule: never use `weixin,origin` when origin is the same weixin account — always explicit single channel; keep ≥15min between must-push morning crons.**

## Live signal (Phase 4)
- `signal_daily.py` computes today's DSA signal (买入/持有/卖出/观望) from latest data, outputs plain text.
